<p class="page-kicker">Consent Knowledge Base</p>
<h1 class="page-title">How we handle your data</h1>
<p>This page explains how AussieBankFeeds collects, uses, stores, and protects your banking data under Australia's Consumer Data Right (CDR), and how you can review, update, or withdraw your consent at any time.</p>
<p class="page-subtitle">Last updated: 23 April 2026</p>

<h2 id="cdr">1. Introduction to the Consumer Data Right (CDR)</h2>
<p>The Consumer Data Right (CDR) is an Australian framework that regulates how consumer data (including banking data) is collected, shared, and protected. It gives you greater control over your own data and sets strict privacy and security standards that every participant in the system must follow.</p>

<h3>Why we collect your data</h3>
<p>AussieBankFeeds provides automatic bank feeds for Australian businesses using Manager.io accounting software. With your consent, we collect your transaction and account data from your financial institution for the following specific purposes:</p>
<ul>
    <li>To retrieve your bank transactions and deliver them into your Manager.io accounting software.</li>
    <li>To keep your Manager.io records in sync with your bank accounts on an ongoing basis.</li>
    <li>To show you the status of your connected accounts and transaction imports inside AussieBankFeeds.</li>
    <li>To meet our legal, security, and fraud-prevention obligations as a Basiq partner.</li>
</ul>
<p>We do not sell your data, and we do not use it for advertising, profiling, or any purpose other than those listed above.</p>

<h3>How your data is accessed</h3>
<p>AussieBankFeeds accesses your bank data through <a href="https://basiq.io" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Basiq</a>, an Accredited Data Recipient (ADR) approved to handle consumer banking data under the CDR. Basiq facilitates the secure connection between your bank and AussieBankFeeds so that you never need to share your banking credentials with us.</p>

<h3>Accredited Data Recipients (ADRs)</h3>
<p>ADRs are organisations that have been formally accredited to receive and manage consumer data under the CDR regime. They are required to:</p>
<ul>
    <li>Disclose clearly what data they collect and how it will be used.</li>
    <li>Store data securely using industry-standard encryption and access controls.</li>
    <li>Implement privacy safeguards that meet or exceed the CDR requirements.</li>
    <li>Allow consumers to view, modify, or withdraw their consent at any time.</li>
</ul>

<h3>Your rights</h3>
<ul>
    <li>You choose which accounts to share and for how long.</li>
    <li>You can modify or withdraw your consent at any time from inside AussieBankFeeds.</li>
    <li>You can request that your data be deleted or de-identified when you withdraw consent.</li>
    <li>You can contact us with questions or complaints about how your data is handled.</li>
</ul>

<h2 id="consent-management">2. Managing your consent</h2>
<p>You are always in control of your data. You can review, update, or withdraw your consent at any time using either of the methods below.</p>

<div class="card">
    <h3>Option A — Inside AussieBankFeeds</h3>
    <ol>
        <li>Sign in to your account at <a href="{{ site.app }}">app.aussiebankfeeds.com</a>.</li>
        <li>Open the <strong>Connections</strong> tab from the top navigation.</li>
        <li>Select the bank connection you want to manage.</li>
        <li>Choose <strong>Review consent</strong> to view what you have shared, or <strong>Withdraw consent</strong> to stop sharing.</li>
    </ol>
    <p>Withdrawing consent immediately stops any further data being collected from that bank connection. Existing transactions that have already been imported into your Manager.io file remain under your control.</p>
</div>

<div class="card">
    <h3>Option B — Contact support</h3>
    <p>If you are unable to access your account, you can also manage your consent by contacting our support team:</p>
    <p><strong>Email:</strong> <a href="mailto:{{ site.email }}">{{ site.email }}</a></p>
    <p>We will respond to consent-related requests within 2 business days and will confirm in writing once any changes have been applied.</p>
</div>

<h3>What you can do</h3>
<ul>
    <li><strong>Review</strong> — see which accounts and data types you have shared, and with whom.</li>
    <li><strong>Modify</strong> — change which accounts are included in the feed.</li>
    <li><strong>Withdraw</strong> — stop all future data sharing for a given connection.</li>
    <li><strong>Request deletion or de-identification</strong> — ask that your previously-shared data be removed or anonymised.</li>
</ul>

<h2 id="contact">3. Contact us</h2>
<p>If you have questions about your consent, how your data is handled, or you wish to make a complaint, please get in touch.</p>
<p><strong>Email:</strong> <a href="mailto:{{ site.email }}">{{ site.email }}</a></p>
<p>You can also raise a complaint directly with the <a href="https://www.oaic.gov.au/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Office of the Australian Information Commissioner (OAIC)</a>.</p>
